Workarounds for older ptxas versions (such as PTXAS 8.7 in CUDA 12.8):

1. Disables 256-bit global load/store vectorization on Blackwell (sm_100+): on
   Blackwell architectures with PTX 8.8+, upstream Triton generates 256-bit
   global memory load and store instructions (e.g. ld.global.v8.b32,
   st.global.v8.b32, ld.global.v4.b64) which older ptxas toolchains fail to
   compile. Capping maxVecBits at 128 bits avoids ptxas compilation failures.
2. Uses inline PTX for FP4-to-FP16 conversion on Blackwell and skips sm_103
   compile-only tests unsupported by CUDA 12.8 ptxas.
3. Passes `--opt-level 1` in `test_dot3d` for the float64 8x32x32x32 2-warp
   case on sm_80 when ptxas < 12.9: ptxas 12.8 miscompiles this kernel at
   -O2/-O3 by collapsing to 32 registers and clobbering a shared-memory offset
   register before `IMAD.SHL`, producing misaligned `LDS.64` addresses (fixed
   in ptxas >= 12.9).

